    "narrative": "The Austin Waves lineup for May 31, 2026, is headlined by **Jackson Merrill** (75.27) and **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (73.66), our two highest-projected starters today. **Jackson Merrill** benefits significantly from a favorable matchup against Littell, whose 4.63 xERA invites high-volume production, while his position in the heart of the order provides ample RBI opportunities. Meanwhile, **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** capitalizes on a strong platoon edge against Canning; his dynamic platoon adjustment (+14%) and favorable park factors solidify his role as a daily anchor. **Gunnar Henderson** and **Kyle Tucker** also offer elite output (70.51 and 70.98, respectively), providing the necessary power-speed foundation to keep our 5x5 categories competitive despite the difficult matchup against Andrew Painter.\n\nRegarding bench decisions, **Liam Hicks** (39.58) remains the most notable exclusion, falling just fractions of a point shy of our 40.0-point floor. While his +11% platoon adjustment against McLean was enticing, the combination of a tough 3.03 xERA and park penalties ultimately kept him on the pine. We are monitoring the situation with **Andy Pages** and **Kyle Tucker** closely, as their statuses remain \"Lineup Pending.\" Should either be scratched, we will need to reassess our utility depth, though we are currently comfortable with the upside provided by **Sam Antonacci** (66.09), who is slated to leadoff and remains a vital source of stolen bases given his strong xwOBA.\n\nWe maintain a cautious outlook on **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (56.40), whose score is suppressed by a difficult assignment against Bradish (3.09 xERA). While his 16% park factor cushion prevents a deeper slide, he is a candidate for underperformance today if the matchup turns into a pitcher's duel. We are also keeping a close eye on the bottom of the order, specifically **Brayan Rocchio** (40.91), whose proximity to the floor serves as a reminder that we are prioritizing defensive stability and stolen base upside today, even at the cost of some offensive volatility against Suarez.",
